  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "3a+jQlHuERZ+oeC7wbLXqElt8Mo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:25:52.208Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The UK entity of GFT is recorded with banking-only positioning aimed at tier-1 banks, and that is what excludes it. Banking is not itself a bad vertical for an append-only decision record \u2014 the opposite, since approval provenance is already a funded question there. The problem is the tier: tier-1 bank programmes are long, committee-driven procurements where a first design-partner engagement cannot realistically be placed.\n\nAs with several rows in this cohort, the tool column reads not researched, so the platform-level screen never ran. The exclusion is therefore positional only, and rests on segment rather than on stack or open-source posture.\n\nWorth noting alongside this: the German parent, GFT Technologies SE, appears elsewhere in the same corpus as a Flowable partner holding Camunda Platinum certification twice over, ranked priority 3 rather than 9. The same corporate group therefore carries two very different verdicts depending on which national entity the row describes \u2014 a reminder that these screens are entity-level, not group-level, and that a do-not-pitch on one row does not close the group.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- GFT UK (UK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Banking-only positioning, tier-1 banks.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:25:52.208355Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:25:52.208397Z"
    }
  },
